-- Q2861: Legal Duties and Responsibilities [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the Restatement (Second) of Torts, Section 299A, a CPA owes a duty to exercise the skill and care that a reasonably competent practitioner would exercise under similar circumstances. This is an objective standard based on professional norms, not a guarantee of perfection.
Wrong (A): A CPA does not guarantee accuracy. The negligence standard requires only reasonable care, not a warranty against all errors.
Wrong (B): CPAs are not required to achieve the best possible outcome. The duty is to exercise reasonable professional care, not to optimize results.
Wrong (C): The standard is that of a reasonably competent practitioner, not the most experienced. Measuring against elite practitioners would impose an unreasonably high bar.$EXPL$
