-- Q2862: Legal Duties and Responsibilities [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under common law as articulated in Ultramares Corp. v. Touche and Restatement (Second) of Torts, Section 552, establishing CPA negligence requires proof of four elements: (1) a duty of care existed, (2) the CPA breached that duty, (3) the breach proximately caused harm, and (4) the plaintiff suffered actual damages.
Wrong (B): Proving only that an error occurred is insufficient. The plaintiff must also establish duty, causation, and damages.
Wrong (C): Intentional harm is the standard for fraud, not negligence. Negligence requires only a failure to exercise due professional care.
Wrong (D): Lack of proper licensing may support other claims but is not the standard for proving negligence in an audit engagement.$EXPL$
