-- Q2863: Legal Duties and Responsibilities [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under the Ultramares doctrine (Ultramares Corp. v. Touche, 1931), consistent with Restatement (Second) of Torts Section 552, an accountant''s liability for negligence is limited to parties in privity of contract and intended third-party beneficiaries. This is the most restrictive standard, protecting accountants from indeterminate liability to unknown users.
Wrong (A): The foreseeable users standard is the broadest approach (Rosenblum v. Adler), not the Ultramares doctrine. Ultramares requires a direct or near-contractual relationship.
Wrong (C): Extending liability to any person who relies on the work for any purpose would create unlimited exposure, which Ultramares specifically rejected.
Wrong (D): The SEC and all investors standard applies under federal securities law, not under the common-law Ultramares privity doctrine.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 2863;

