-- Q2870: Legal Duties and Responsibilities [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the Restatement (Second) of Torts, Section 552, a CPA is liable for negligence to foreseen users, meaning specifically identified third parties or members of a limited class the accountant knows will rely on the work. The supplier was identified by name during the engagement, making them a specifically foreseen user.
Wrong (A): Under the Restatement approach, a foreseen user need not be a party to the engagement. Being specifically identified as a user of the statements is sufficient.
Wrong (B): The Restatement approach extends liability beyond strict privity to foreseen users, unlike the more restrictive Ultramares doctrine.
Wrong (C): Fraud is not required under the Restatement approach. A negligence claim is sufficient when the plaintiff is a foreseen user of the financial statements.$EXPL$
