-- Q2871: Legal Duties and Responsibilities [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C Section 200 and common law negligence principles, having work reviewed by another CPA is not a recognized defense to a negligence claim. Peer review addresses quality control but does not excuse the individual CPA''s professional responsibility.
Wrong (A): Contributory negligence is a valid defense. If the client''s own conduct contributed to the loss, it may reduce or bar recovery.
Wrong (B): Lack of duty owed to the plaintiff is a valid defense. If no duty of care exists, the negligence claim fails on the first element.
Wrong (C): Compliance with GAAS and GAAP is a valid defense under AU-C standards, demonstrating the CPA met the applicable standard of care.$EXPL$
