  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Circular 230 Section 10.50, a practitioner who engages in disreputable conduct, including knowingly making false statements on tax returns, may be censured, suspended, or disbarred from practice before the IRS. These administrative sanctions are imposed by the Office of Professional Responsibility.
Wrong (B): Criminal imprisonment is imposed under IRC Section 7206 for tax fraud, not under Circular 230. Circular 230 provides administrative sanctions only.
Wrong (C): State license revocation is handled by state boards of accountancy, not under Circular 230. Circular 230 governs practice before the IRS specifically.
