Wrong (A): Material misrepresentation must still be proven in a constructive fraud claim. It is an essential element, not one that is waived.
Wrong (B): Reliance by the plaintiff remains a required element. The plaintiff must show justifiable reliance on the CPA''s misrepresentation.
