  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 10(b) and Rule 10b-5 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, private plaintiffs must prove scienter, meaning intent to deceive, manipulate, or defraud. Most courts interpret this to include recklessness amounting to a conscious disregard of risk. Mere negligence is insufficient under federal securities law.
Wrong (A): Simple negligence does not meet the mental state requirement for a Rule 10b-5 claim. The standard requires intentional or reckless conduct.
Wrong (B): Strict liability does not apply under Section 10(b). A mental state element (scienter) is always required for private plaintiffs.
