-- Q2888: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 507 of the Bankruptcy Code, the priority order is: (1) domestic support obligations, (2) administrative expenses, (3) gap claims, (4) employee wages, (5) benefit plan contributions, (6) grain/fishermen claims, (7) consumer deposits, (8) tax claims. General unsecured creditors come after all priority claims.
Wrong (A): General unsecured creditors are paid last, not first. Wage claims and tax claims both have priority status above general unsecured debt.
Wrong (B): Administrative expenses rank second, not first. Domestic support obligations hold the highest priority under Section 507(a)(1).
Wrong (D): Secured creditors are paid from their collateral before the priority distribution. Priority claims are paid before general unsecured creditors, not after.$EXPL$
