-- Q2889: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the Restatement (Third) of Suretyship and Guaranty, Section 72, when a surety pays the creditor upon the debtor''s default, the surety obtains the right of subrogation, stepping into the creditor''s legal position to pursue the debtor for reimbursement. This right arises by operation of law upon payment.
Wrong (A): The surety does not forfeit all rights by guaranteeing the debt. Payment upon default triggers legal rights including subrogation and reimbursement.
Wrong (B): The surety is entitled to recover the full amount paid, not merely 50%. Subrogation gives the surety the creditor''s full rights against the debtor.
Wrong (C): The surety recovers only the amount actually paid, not double. Punitive or multiplied recovery is not a feature of suretyship law.$EXPL$
